application security triage: Server-Side Request Forgery via Webhook Validator (CWE-918) A SaaS platform lets users register a webhook URL and 'test' it server-side; the test function fetches the URL directly without restricting destination IP ranges or schemes. Monitor outbound requests initiated by server-side fetch utilities for destinations in RFC1918, loopback, and link-local ranges; flag non-HTTP(S) schemes (file://, gopher://, dict://) in user-supplied URLs; alert on repeated webhook URL changes within short time windows from a single account. def validate_webhook_url(url):
    parsed = urlparse(url)
    if parsed.scheme not in ('http','https'):
        raise ValueError('Invalid scheme')
    ip = ipaddress.ip_address(socket.gethostbyname(parsed.hostname))
    if ip.is_private or ip.is_loopback or ip.is_link_local or ip.is_reserved:
        raise ValueError('Blocked internal destination')
    return True 198.51.100.63 - - [04/Oct/2026:11:15:40 +0000] "POST /api/webhooks/test HTTP/1.1" 200 756 "-" "curl/8.4.0" body={"url":"http://169.254.169.254/latest/meta-data/iam/security-credentials/"}

