defensive review: Insecure Direct Object Reference - IDOR (CWE-639) A billing API exposes invoice details at /api/invoices/{id} using a sequential integer primary key, and the authorization check only verifies that the requester is logged in, not that they own the specific invoice. Detect sequential or near-sequential resource ID access patterns from a single authenticated session in a short time window; cross-reference requested resource owner ID against authenticated user ID at the log level; flag high-velocity enumeration (>N requests/minute to a parameterized ID endpoint). @app.get('/api/invoices/{invoice_id}')
def get_invoice(invoice_id: int, current_user: User = Depends(get_current_user)):
    invoice = db.get_invoice(invoice_id)
    if invoice.owner_id != current_user.id:
        raise HTTPException(status_code=403, detail='Forbidden')
    return invoice 192.0.2.201 - - [04/Oct/2026:09:40:02 +0000] "GET /api/invoices/4471 HTTP/1.1" 200 1890 "-" "Mozilla/5.0" Authorization: Bearer eyJhbGciOi...user4471

